## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation, I:
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Placed the `<Analytics />` component at the root level to track all pages
- Maintained existing code structure and patterns
- Preserved all existing functionality

## Next Steps for Deployment

To activate Vercel Web Analytics:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
2. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy` or push to your connected Git repository
3. Verify tracking by checking the Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

## Framework-Specific Notes

This project uses TanStack Start, which is a React-based full-stack framework. The Analytics component was added to the `RootComponent` in `__root.tsx`, which serves as the application shell and wraps all routes. This ensures analytics tracking works correctly for:
- Initial page loads
- Client-side navigation
- All nested routes rendered through `<Outlet />`
